The `Android Client` job on audit PRs #83 and #85 receives a runner and starts normally, but
fails in `android-actions/setup-android@v4.0.1` before any repository Gradle task runs.

The pinned action's `action.yml` defaults `packages` to `tools platform-tools`. The legacy SDK
package `tools` is no longer available, so `sdkmanager` exits with `Failed to find package
'tools'`. This is not a GitHub API or Actions run-rate-limit failure.

## Scope

- `.github/workflows/ci-basic.yml`
- `.github/workflows/android-instrumentation.yml`

## Proposed bounded correction

- Override the action input with `packages: platform-tools` in both workflows.
- Retain the existing explicit install of API 36, Build Tools 36, CMake, and NDK.
- Do not change Gradle, Android source, signing, deployment, or release behavior in this task.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Both workflows complete `Set up Android SDK` without requesting package `tools`.
- [ ] The jobs reach the repository Gradle commands.
- [ ] Basic CI Android Client passes on an exact candidate head.
- [ ] Instrumentation reaches and passes the API 24/API 36 matrix, or any later failure is
      separately demonstrated to be repository/test behavior rather than SDK bootstrap.
- [ ] Existing security and dependency checks remain green.
- [ ] The audit PRs are rerun only after the workflow correction is merged.

