## Context

PR #85 contains useful real-device measurements from a 320dp S10 and a Tab S4, and the owner
reported three additional S10 defects. This issue groups the later UI implementation without
mixing it into the security/crypto findings in #84.

Important correction: current source already defines `android:minHeight=64dp` for dial keys.
The measured 42dp key height may still be real in the shipped 1.0.48 artifact, but adding a
48dp minimum is not the correct diagnosis. The fix must start with exact-source measurement.

## Scope

- Bottom navigation labels and touch height on narrow phones.
- Dial-pad measurement and the clipped/invisible `+` below key 0.
- Contact-match rows obscured while the software keyboard is open.
- Settings row touch targets.
- Responsive phone/tablet/landscape constraints and automated viewport checks.
- Direct-Premium standalone VPN settings should expand and collapse like peer sections.
- Release logging/direct-APK ABI hygiene remains a separate informational subtask.

## Source facts already confirmed

- `MainActivity` uses `windowSoftInputMode="adjustPan"`.
- Bottom navigation has no explicit label visibility mode or stable minimum height.
- The dial pad is height/row-weight driven and key 0 uses a two-line `0\n+` label.
- The Premium VPN block is dynamically appended as a plain `PreferenceCategory`, while the
  normal settings sections use `CollapsiblePreferenceCategory`.
- No screen-size or landscape layout/value qualifiers exist.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] At 320dp width, all four bottom-navigation labels remain readable and all targets are
      at least 48dp.
- [ ] All twelve dial keys measure at least 48x48dp on an exact-source build; the existing
      64dp source floor is not reduced without measurement evidence.
- [ ] `0` and `+` remain visible at default and enlarged font scales.
